as, como precios de mercado o necesidades específicas.\nQué se puede revisar: Es importante comprobar si los contratos [1] y [2] atienden la misma necesidad. También revisar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en distintas áreas. Verificar si los contratos de diciembre se relacionan con otros adjudicados en el mismo periodo.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 81 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 11.4 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 7.1, with a 95% confidence interval of 5.0 to 10.2. December accounts for 5% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 3% of all its services and supplies contracts. The contracts just under the limit are spread across 67 different awardees. Contract [1], for 14,990 euros, was awarded in September 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts near the legal limit does not prove improper actions. It could reflect market conditions, budget constraints, or separate needs. Statistical patterns alone do not indicate wrongdoing without further investigation.\nWhat can be checked: Check the distribution of contracts across awardees to identify patterns. Review the specific services purchased in each contract to ensure they align with the body's needs. Examine if multiple contracts served the same purpose to assess potential over-bidding.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["ERyFqCbM2qLzAq95uGTrDQ%3D%3D","%2FwoUKOAbNYmAAM7L03kM8A%3D%3D","dzBJc2SgbiB70UvEyYJSGw%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}